body:
@original-brownbear ^ Does this just look like a I/O error and we re-threw it?

Its weird that there is a 3 second gap from reloading `test` analyzers and IO failing. Something weird. 

None of the other nodes seem to throw anything around this time.

I can't reproduce this locally, tried executing all synonyms related tests with `-Dtests.method="test {p0=synonyms/*}"`. 

This test doesn't seem to have failed in the previous 24 hours:

![image](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/assets/6339205/40d8088f-26a8-4f52-9e0f-d51223cbf768)

@DaveCTurner , have you found other instances of this failing?

Checking the failed node logs, I see there's an error that seems uncaught:

```
2023-11-15T13:22:28,176][WARN ][i.n.c.AbstractChannelHandlerContext] [v8.10.4-1] Failed to mark a promise as failure because it has failed already: DefaultChannelPromise@778c1ae(failure: java.nio.channels.ClosedChannelException), unnotified cause: java.nio.channels.ClosedChannelException
	at org.elasticsearch.transport.netty4@8.12.0-SNAPSHOT/org.elasticsearch.http.netty4.Netty4HttpPipeliningHandler.write(Netty4HttpPipeliningHandler.java:168)
	at io.netty.transport@4.1.94.Final/io.netty.channel.AbstractChannelHandlerContext.invokeWrite0(AbstractChannelHandlerContext.java:879)
```

this is related to [this code](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/47641341051c7d52ed218d501ac45467a41c971d/modules/transport-netty4/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/http/netty4/Netty4HttpPipeliningHandler.java#L168):

```java
        } finally {
            if (success == false) {
                promise.setFailure(new ClosedChannelException());
            }
        }
```

Should we change that to:
```java
        } finally {
            if (success == false) {
                safeFailPromise(promise, new ClosedChannelException());
            }
        }

```

so we ensure that we don't die even if the promise is already failed?
